14sa|n|The workroom of a chemist; also, a place devoted to experiments in any branch of natural science; as, a chemical, physical, or biological laboratory. Hence, by extension, a place where something is prepared, or some operation is performed; as, the liver is the laboratory of the bile.	a:1bx9,79,34;7rs,68,3;1imv,46,5;1cdz,1,2;1era,0,4~1bx9,79,34;1imv,46,5;1era,0,4;7rs,68,3;1cdz,1,2	n:jls,46,3;1in7,32,4;edl,17,3;25l6,11,4~1in7,32,4;25l6,11,4;jls,46,3;edl,17,3	N:110p,85,3;qti,80,7;1czc,79,4;1zmf,77,3;p52,66,8;1wcr,46,5;21im,44,3;ork,43,4;d1g,28,3;1sk6,22,6~p52,66,8;qti,80,7;1sk6,22,6;qdb,21,5;1wcr,46,5;ork,43,4;1czc,79,4;21im,44,3;d1g,28,3;htb,15,3
14sf|a|Requiring labor, perseverance, or sacrifices; toilsome; tiresome. ; Devoted to labor; diligent; industrious; as, a laborious mechanic.	e:xvw,63,3;2753,30,4;1awf,24,4~1awf,24,4;2753,30,4;xvw,63,3
